  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P164_is_temporally_specified_by">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="ru">ограничиваeтся врeмeнeм</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">is temporally specified by</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="fr">est temporellement spécifié par</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P164i_temporally_specifies"/>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E93_Presence"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E52_Time-Span"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This property relates an instance of E93 Presence with the instance of E52 Time-Span that defines the time-slice of the spacetime volume that this instance of E93 Presence is related to via the property P166 was a presence of (had presence).
There are two typical cases for the determination of the related instance of E52 Time-Span. In the first, it is the temporal extent of an instance of E2 Temporal Entity (documented with P4 has time-span (is time-span of)): this then documents the simultaneity of the instance of E93 Presence and the instance of E2 Temporal Entity, even if the absolute time-span is not known, and can be regarded as a phenomenal time-span. In the second, the instance of E52 Time-Span is a date range declared in or derived from historical sources or provided by dating methods: this is a declarative time-span.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P160_has_temporal_projection"/>
  </rdf:Description>
